    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>It's not a temporary feeling though. It's getting worse. Every time I forget something, it feels like a piece of \"me\" just dies. I'm terrified that in a year, I'll be sitting in a chair staring at a wall, unable to even hold a conversation. I'd rather just... go out while I still know who I am. Does that sound crazy? To want to leave before the person i love becomes a stranger?",
